  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A light ray enters a solid glass sphere of refractive index&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;at an angle of incidence&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. The ray is both reflected and refracted at the farther surface of the sphere. The angle (in degrees) between the reflected and refracted rays at this surface is _____________.</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "90",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0166_cbd9454a3891.jpg\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 94px;\" /></p><p>Apply Snell&#39;s law at S_<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math><br />from geometry<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math><br />Again apply snell&#39;s law on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><msup><mi>sinr</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>sine</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>sine</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math><br />from geometry<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"
  }
}